		{
			"id": "8nfzq678",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -1274.762338022845,
			"y": -3312.5391798604933,
			"width": 1023.3992309570312,
			"height": 25,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aZ",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 839636726,
			"version": 23,
			"versionNonce": 1974530678,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775088486700,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "In distributed stream processing systems, one of the biggest challenges is handling out-of-order events.",
			"rawText": "In distributed stream processing systems, one of the biggest challenges is handling out-of-order events.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "In distributed stream processing systems, one of the biggest challenges is handling out-of-order events.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "JrEw7dFc",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -1275.1752903507343,
			"y": -3237.7403278233196,
			"width": 1462.963697482927,
			"height": 75,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aa",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1671530550,
			"version": 410,
			"versionNonce": 803608554,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775088486700,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Watermarks are Flink's solution to this problem. A watermark is essentially a timestamp that flows through the system alongside streaming data and\ndeclares \"all events with timestamps before this watermark have arrived.\" As an example, you might receive the watermark that lets you know 5pm\nhas passed at 5:01:15pm.",
			"rawText": "Watermarks are Flink's solution to this problem. A watermark is essentially a timestamp that flows through the system alongside streaming data and declares \"all events with timestamps before this watermark have arrived.\" As an example, you might receive the watermark that lets you know 5pm has passed at 5:01:15pm.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Watermarks are Flink's solution to this problem. A watermark is essentially a timestamp that flows through the system alongside streaming data and declares \"all events with timestamps before this watermark have arrived.\" As an example, you might receive the watermark that lets you know 5pm has passed at 5:01:15pm.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
