		{
			"id": "WJ87LP0W",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -1283.4558992501627,
			"y": 1542.1912362699748,
			"width": 1374.8097398345465,
			"height": 120,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0R",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1742447222,
			"version": 134,
			"versionNonce": 524155958,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775088486700,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Job Manager and Task Managers\n\nFlink runs as a distributed system with two main types of processes:\n- Job Manager is the coordinator of the Flink cluster. It's responsible for scheduling tasks, coordinating checkpoints, and handling failures. Think of it as the \"supervisor\" of\nthe operation.\n- Task Managers are the workers that execute the actual data processing. Each Task Manager provides a certain number of processing slots to the cluster.",
			"rawText": "Job Manager and Task Managers\n\nFlink runs as a distributed system with two main types of processes:\n- Job Manager is the coordinator of the Flink cluster. It's responsible for scheduling tasks, coordinating checkpoints, and handling failures. Think of it as the \"supervisor\" of the operation.\n- Task Managers are the workers that execute the actual data processing. Each Task Manager provides a certain number of processing slots to the cluster.",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Job Manager and Task Managers\n\nFlink runs as a distributed system with two main types of processes:\n- Job Manager is the coordinator of the Flink cluster. It's responsible for scheduling tasks, coordinating checkpoints, and handling failures. Think of it as the \"supervisor\" of the operation.\n- Task Managers are the workers that execute the actual data processing. Each Task Manager provides a certain number of processing slots to the cluster.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
